      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Writing n^{-it} as oscillation in log n identifies Dirichlet data as transform-like; the Mellin/Perron kernel converts each ratio x/n into a threshold, and summing that kernel against coefficients yields a truncated inversion formula whose von Mangoldt specialization turns Psi into an integral of -zeta'/zeta that can be attacked by contour deformation.",
