      "proposed_content": "Prime-local positivity first yields a weak zero-free region; a general growth-to-zero-exclusion transfer widens the available strip, local control of zeta'/zeta makes that wider strip usable, and the extra leftward contour displacement reduces x^{Re(s)}, so optimizing the contour height converts zero-free width into a stronger error term for Psi.",
